+    Founder's ask (2026-09-15, the Omni-State Hypervisor synthesis): a semantic code graph
+    alongside the runtime one, without a second store or a SCIP toolchain this estate does not
+    have. What this can honestly claim: for every git-tracked `.py` file, one `code:module:*`
+    node (id = dotted module path, e.g. `code:module:sovereign.verifier`), and one `imports`
+    edge per `import`/`from ... import ...` statement whose target resolves EXACTLY to another
+    module already in this same set. A resolvable-but-external import (stdlib, a pip package)
+    is not recorded as an edge to nowhere; an id namespace of its own (`code:module:`) keeps
